# Project: StackForge

## Stack
Python 3.10+ CLI (`stackforge-cli` on PyPI, `stackforge` command), setuptools, colorama. Scaffolds .NET 10 Clean Architecture (CQRS) projects.

## Architecture
Single CLI entry (`stackforge.scaffold:main`) delegating to engine modules under `src/stackforge/engines/dotnet/`. Each generator owns one artifact type (csproj, docker, git, API, layers, config).

## Naming & Conventions
- Python: snake_case modules/functions, PascalCase for .NET project names
- Generated .NET: PascalCase layers (API, Application, Domain, Infrastructure, Persistence)
- Scaffold output path: `~/stackforge/{ProjectName}`

## Key Constraints
- Only .NET Clean Architecture is implemented; other frameworks are placeholders
- Git default branch must be `main` (not `master`)
- Environment branches: `staging`, `development`

## Folder Structure
```
src/stackforge/
  scaffold.py          # CLI entry
  engines/dotnet/      # .NET scaffolder + generators
```

## What NOT to Do
- Do not use `master` as the default branch name
- Do not add framework scaffolds without implementing the full generator set
- Match existing generator pattern: one file per concern, called from `scaffolder.py`
